  "description": "Issue #50 / #47. ONE connection in the default library (<USER>2). Derived from part04v-27set (same CLONEDIR staging of the legacy tree). PRECOND: DBVER=1. Compiles the FIXED tools/qclsrc/txlegacy.clp, then (1) TXLEGACY LANG(*RPGLE) FORCE(*YES) from a clean start (SAVOBJ to <USER>B appears in the TXLEGACY job log lines in VFYLOG); (2) applies ticket 1 to JU0900C (source before/after copied to V27SB/V27SA); (3) sets TXLEGST to N and runs FORCE(*YES) again: issue #47 expects TXLEGST back to Y, and JU0900C source back to LEN(3 0) (V27SR), the lesson claim that FORCE(*YES) undoes the ticket 1 fix. LAST: restore the RPG III legacy system (TXLEGST/TXLEGLNG deleted, LANG(*RPG), no FORCE) and TXRESET. HONEST LIMITS: single-library simulation; V3 steps not covered.",
